TransAmiga v1.1 Programmer's Reference:
---------------------------------------

This archive should contain the files:

    Docs/trans_lib.doc       (autodoc style manual for transamiga.library)
    Docs/Tech.doc            (technical info on TransAmiga's file formats)
    transamiga.h             (TransAmiga header file)
    transamiga_protos.h      (prototypes for the library)
    transamiga_lib.fd        (FD file of transamiga.library functions)
    TrShell.c                (source for TrShell)
    Prog.Read_Me             (this file)

Be sure that everything is in its proper sub-directory.

Users of SAS C and Aztec C will need to generate #pragma calls for all the
library functions from the included .fd file using tools provided with
each compiler.  DICE users will need to create a .lib from the .fd file
using the FDtoLib command.

These files are intended only for those wishing to write doors and
utilities for use with TransAmiga BBS.  They're of a technical nature, so
if you don't know what you're doing, they won't be of much use to you.


-Tim

